/* =====================================================================
   Short Bowel Syndrome with Chronic Intestinal Failure (SBS-IF)
   Short Bowel Syndrome · Chronic Intestinal Failure — QSP Mechanistic Map
   ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   THE ORGANISING IDEA

     SBS-IF IS NOT A DISEASE OF A MISSING ORGAN. IT IS A DISEASE OF AN
     UNCLOSED MASS BALANCE. THE THING THE CLINICIAN PRESCRIBES —
     PARENTERAL SUPPORT — IS NOT A TREATMENT INTENSITY. IT IS THE
     ARITHMETIC RESIDUAL OF TWO CONSERVATION EQUATIONS.

   Almost every other model in this library has a disease severity state
   that a drug pushes down and a clinical score that follows it. SBS-IF
   is structurally different, and the difference is the whole point:

     PN VOLUME IS AN OUTPUT, NOT AN INPUT.

   A patient with 70 cm of jejunum ending in a stoma is not "sick" in
   the sense that a lupus patient is sick. Their mucosa is histologically
   near-normal. What has failed is a budget:

       FLUID :  intake + secretions  −  absorbed  =  output
                output + urine + insensible − oral absorbed  =  DEFICIT
                DEFICIT must be filled from a central vein.

       ENERGY:  oral kcal x absorptive coefficient + colonic SCFA salvage
                − total energy expenditure  =  DEFICIT
                DEFICIT must be filled from a central vein.

   Every arrow on this map earns its place by changing one of the terms
   in those two equations. A drug that raises villus height matters only
   because villus height raises the absorptive coefficient; the villus
   is not the endpoint, the litre is.

   ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   WHY THIS MAKES THE PHARMACOLOGY FALL OUT RATHER THAN BE ASSERTED

   FOUR consequences follow from taking the balance seriously, and all
   four are clinical facts that a severity-score model cannot generate:

     1. THE JEJUNUM SECRETES. Jejunal mucosa is the leakiest epithelium
        in the gut. Net water flux there is not "absorption with some
        loss" — it reverses sign. Sodium absorption is zero at luminal
        [Na+] near 90-100 mmol/L and NEGATIVE below it, because water
        follows the osmotic gradient into a hypotonic lumen dragging
        sodium with it. So a thirsty end-jejunostomy patient who drinks
        two litres of water LOSES sodium and volume, and the same patient
        given two litres of glucose-saline at 90 mmol/L Na+ GAINS both.
        This is the single most counter-intuitive fact in the disease and
        it is a sign change in one flux equation, not a warning label.

     2. THE COLON IS A DIGESTIVE ORGAN. A colon in continuity absorbs up
        to 3-4 L of water and 400-800 mmol of sodium per day, and ferments
        unabsorbed carbohydrate to short-chain fatty acids worth up to
        ~1000 kcal/day. This is why the anatomical thresholds for
        permanent intestinal failure differ almost threefold between
        anatomies (end-jejunostomy ~115 cm, jejunocolic ~60 cm,
        jejuno-ileo-colic ~35 cm). Anatomy is therefore a PARAMETER on
        this map that multiplies capacities, never a severity label.

     3. THE ILEAL BRAKE IS THE LOOP THAT CLOSES ON ITSELF. GLP-2, GLP-1,
        PYY and neurotensin come from L-cells, and L-cells live in the
        distal ileum and proximal colon — precisely the tissue most
        often resected. Losing them removes the feedback that slows
        gastric emptying and small-bowel transit. Faster transit means
        less mucosal contact time, less contact time means less
        absorption, less absorption means more unabsorbed load, and the
        L-cells that would have sensed it are gone. THE POSITIVE
        FEEDBACK IS WHY THE DISEASE IS SELF-SUSTAINING, and supplying
        exogenous GLP-2 is an attempt to re-close a broken loop rather
        than to suppress an overactive one.

     4. ADAPTATION IS NUTRIENT-GATED, SO THE DRUG NEEDS FOOD. Structural
        adaptation (villus height, crypt proliferation, mucosal mass) is
        driven by luminal nutrient contact acting THROUGH the same
        enterohormonal axis. A patient kept nil-by-mouth on full PN does
        not adapt, and — the part that matters pharmacologically — does
        not respond to a GLP-2 analogue either, because the trophic
        signal is drawn here as a PRODUCT of luminal nutrient and
        receptor occupancy, not a sum. Trophic feeding is not adjunctive
        comfort; it is a multiplicand.

   ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   THE WEANING ALGORITHM IS PART OF THE PATHOPHYSIOLOGY

   One further structural choice, unusual enough to state plainly. In the
   STEPS trial the investigator did not choose the PN reduction; a
   protocol did. PN volume was cut when 24-hour URINE OUTPUT rose ≥10%
   above baseline, because rising urine is the observable signature of a
   closed fluid balance. That algorithm is drawn on this map as a real
   feedback controller (cluster PN), which means:

     - the drug's effect on the registered endpoint (≥20% PN volume
       reduction) is produced by simulating the PROTOCOL, not by fitting
       a PN-reduction parameter;
     - and the placebo arm's substantial "response" emerges as a
       property of the algorithm itself — any patient carrying unused
       absorptive reserve will be weaned by a urine-triggered protocol
       whether or not they received drug. The placebo response in SBS
       trials is partly an artefact of good protocolised care.

   ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   WHAT KILLS THESE PATIENTS IS THE THERAPY'S PLUMBING, NOT THE BOWEL

   The right-hand third of the map is deliberately given to iatrogenic
   organ injury, because in modern SBS-IF that is where mortality lives:
   intestinal failure-associated liver disease driven by phytosterol load
   and choline deficiency from the lipid emulsion; catheter-related
   bloodstream infection consuming central venous access one vein at a
   time until transplantation becomes the only option; enteric
   hyperoxaluria that requires a colon to happen at all; and metabolic
   bone disease from divalent cation losses. These are not side notes.
   The competing-risk structure — bowel improving while liver and veins
   deteriorate — is the actual decision problem.

   ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   LAYOUT

     Left    ANAT ETIO CAP SECR    anatomy, cause, capacity, secretory load
     Centre  JEJ COLON NRG BAL     the two conservation equations
     Upper   LCELL MOT ADAPT FUNC  the loop and its trophic output
     Lower   BILE MICRO MICRO2     bile acids, bacteria, micronutrients
     Right   PN GLP2PK DRUG        prescription, GLP-2 analogues, adjuncts
     Far-R   IFALD CVC RENAL BONE  iatrogenic organ injury
     Bottom  ENDP TX               endpoints and transplantation

   Node shapes / colours
     box, blue        anatomy & parameters (not states)
     ellipse, grey    physiological fluxes and pools
     ellipse, green   adaptive / protective processes
     ellipse, red     maladaptive / injurious processes
     hexagon, orange  drugs and prescribed inputs
     diamond, purple  clinical endpoints
     octagon, gold    conservation-equation nodes (the balance itself)
     doubleoctagon    structural nulls / traps (effect must be ZERO or REVERSE)

   Edge semantics
     solid arrow       mass flux or causal activation
     dashed arrow      signal / regulation
     dotted arrow      measurement or surveillance
     tee (odiamond)    inhibition
     bold red          the self-sustaining positive feedback loop
   ===================================================================== */

digraph SBS_QSP {
    graph [rankdir=LR, splines=spline, overlap=false, nodesep=0.28, ranksep=1.05,
           fontname="Helvetica", fontsize=11, newrank=true,
           labelloc="t", labeljust="l",
           label=<<B>Short Bowel Syndrome with Chronic Intestinal Failure (SBS-IF) — QSP Mechanistic Map</B><BR/>
<FONT POINT-SIZE="12">Short Bowel Syndrome · Chronic Intestinal Failure — Quantitative Systems Pharmacology mechanistic map</FONT><BR/>
<FONT POINT-SIZE="10">Parenteral support volume is an OUTPUT of two conservation equations (fluid, energy), not an input.<BR/>
Anatomy is a parameter that multiplies capacity. The ileal-brake loop is the positive feedback that makes the disease self-sustaining.<BR/>
Adaptation is nutrient-GATED, so GLP-2 analogue effect enters as a PRODUCT with luminal nutrient — never as a sum.</FONT>>];

    node [fontname="Helvetica", fontsize=9, style="filled", penwidth=1.1];
    edge [fontname="Helvetica", fontsize=8, arrowsize=0.65, color="#555555"];

    /* ============================================================
       CLUSTER 1 — ETIOLOGY: WHY THE BOWEL IS SHORT
       ============================================================ */
    subgraph cluster_ETIO {
        label=<<B>1. Etiology of massive resection</B><BR/><FONT POINT-SIZE="8">the cause sets the remnant, the remnant sets everything else</FONT>>;
        style="filled"; fillcolor="#f2f6fb"; color="#5b7fa6"; fontsize=11;
        node [shape=box, fillcolor="#dbe7f3", color="#5b7fa6"];

        E_MESENT   [label="Acute superior mesenteric artery\nischaemia · embolism\n(adult SBS ~30-40%)"];
        E_VOLV     [label="Midgut volvulus"];
        E_CROHN    [label="Crohn disease\nrepeated resections"];
        E_TRAUMA   [label="Trauma · penetrating\nabdominal injury"];
        E_RADIAT   [label="Radiation enteritis\n(mucosa also injured)"];
        E_NEC      [label="Neonatal necrotising enterocolitis\n(paediatric SBS ~1st cause)"];
        E_ATRESIA  [label="Intestinal atresia /\ngastroschisis"];
        E_DESMOID  [label="Desmoid / intra-abdominal tumour"];
        E_ADHES    [label="Recurrent adhesive obstruction,\nrepeated operations"];
        E_PSEUDO   [label="Chronic intestinal pseudo-obstruction (CIPO)\nfunctional short bowel\n— length NORMAL, motility absent"];

        E_MESENT -> E_RESECT; E_VOLV -> E_RESECT; E_CROHN -> E_RESECT;
        E_TRAUMA -> E_RESECT; E_RADIAT -> E_RESECT; E_NEC -> E_RESECT;
        E_ATRESIA -> E_RESECT; E_DESMOID -> E_RESECT; E_ADHES -> E_RESECT;
        E_RESECT   [label="Massive small-bowel resection", shape=box, fillcolor="#c3d6e8"];
    }

    /* ============================================================
       CLUSTER 2 — ANATOMY AS PARAMETER
       ============================================================ */
    subgraph cluster_ANAT {
        label=<<B>2. Remnant anatomy as PARAMETER</B><BR/><FONT POINT-SIZE="8">these are not states; they multiply every capacity downstream</FONT>>;
        style="filled"; fillcolor="#eef4fa"; color="#3f6d99"; fontsize=11;
        node [shape=box, fillcolor="#cfe0ef", color="#3f6d99"];

        A_SBL      [label="Remnant small-bowel length SBL\n(cm from duodenojejunal flexure)", fillcolor="#b7d0e6"];
        A_ICV      [label="Ileocaecal valve present? ICV\n(0/1)"];
        A_COLON    [label="Colon in continuity COLONFRAC (0-1)\n(0 = end-jejunostomy)", fillcolor="#b7d0e6"];
        A_ILEUM    [label="Remnant ileum (cm)\n— site of B12, bile acid, L-cells"];
        A_STOMACH  [label="Stomach intact?\n(gastric acid load)"];
        A_TYPE1    [label="Messing type 1\nEnd-jejunostomy\npermanent PN-dependence threshold ~115 cm"];
        A_TYPE2    [label="Messing type 2\nJejuno-colic anastomosis\npermanent PN-dependence threshold ~60 cm"];
        A_TYPE3    [label="Messing type 3\nJejuno-ileo-colic\npermanent PN-dependence threshold ~35 cm"];
        A_MUCQUAL  [label="Remnant mucosal quality\n(radiation / Crohn / normal)"];
        A_DILAT    [label="Dilated stagnant loop\n(bacterial reservoir)"];
        A_SURFACE  [label="Effective absorptive surface\n= SBL x villus x microvillus", fillcolor="#9fc2de"];

        A_SBL -> A_TYPE1 [style=invis]; A_COLON -> A_TYPE2 [style=invis];
        A_SBL -> A_SURFACE; A_MUCQUAL -> A_SURFACE;
        A_ICV -> A_DILAT [label="loss →", style=dashed];
        E_RESECT -> A_SBL; E_RESECT -> A_ILEUM; E_RESECT -> A_COLON; E_RESECT -> A_ICV;
        E_PSEUDO -> A_SURFACE [label="normal length,\nzero motility", style=dashed, color="#b03030"];
    }

    /* ============================================================
       CLUSTER 3 — ABSORPTIVE CAPACITY (the coefficient)
       ============================================================ */
    subgraph cluster_CAP {
        label=<<B>3. Absorptive capacity — the Damköhler product</B><BR/><FONT POINT-SIZE="8">absorbed fraction = 1 − exp(−k · surface · contact time): length AND time MULTIPLY</FONT>>;
        style="filled"; fillcolor="#f0f7f0"; color="#4a7a4a"; fontsize=11;
        node [shape=ellipse, fillcolor="#dcecdc", color="#4a7a4a"];

        C_KAPPA    [label="Mucosal permeation constant k\nintrinsic per-area\ntransport constant"];
        C_CONTACT  [label="Mucosal contact time Tc\n(= transit time x mixing)", fillcolor="#c9e2c9"];
        C_DAMK     [label="Damköhler number Da = k·A·Tc\nabsorbed fraction = 1 − e^(−Da)", shape=octagon, fillcolor="#f6e3a0", color="#a08000"];
        C_FRACH2O  [label="Fluid absorption fraction"];
        C_FRACNA   [label="Sodium absorption fraction"];
        C_FRACCHO  [label="Carbohydrate coefficient\nCHO (~0.6-0.9)"];
        C_FRACFAT  [label="Fat coefficient (~0.3-0.7)\nmost length-sensitive", fillcolor="#f5d9d9", color="#a04040"];
        C_FRACPRO  [label="Protein coefficient (~0.6-0.8)"];
        C_SAT      [label="Saturable capacity —\nbigger meals absorbed\nLESS efficiently"];

        A_SURFACE -> C_DAMK; C_KAPPA -> C_DAMK; C_CONTACT -> C_DAMK;
        C_DAMK -> C_FRACH2O; C_DAMK -> C_FRACNA; C_DAMK -> C_FRACCHO;
        C_DAMK -> C_FRACFAT; C_DAMK -> C_FRACPRO;
        C_SAT -> C_FRACCHO [style=dashed, arrowhead=odiamond];
        C_SAT -> C_FRACFAT [style=dashed, arrowhead=odiamond];
    }

    /* ============================================================
       CLUSTER 4 — SECRETORY LOAD (the numerator nobody counts)
       ============================================================ */
    subgraph cluster_SECR {
        label=<<B>4. Endogenous secretory load</B><BR/><FONT POINT-SIZE="8">~6-8 L/day enters the lumen before the patient drinks anything</FONT>>;
        style="filled"; fillcolor="#fdf4ec"; color="#a06a30"; fontsize=11;
        node [shape=ellipse, fillcolor="#f8e3cf", color="#a06a30"];

        S_SALIVA   [label="Saliva\n~1.0-1.5 L/d"];
        S_GASTRIC  [label="Gastric juice\n~1.5-2.5 L/d\n(H+ 150 mmol/L)"];
        S_HYPERSEC [label="Post-resection gastric\nHYPERsecretion\n(loss of inhibitory peptides,\nhypergastrinaemia)", fillcolor="#f5d9d9", color="#a04040"];
        S_BILE     [label="Bile\n~0.5-0.8 L/d"];
        S_PANC     [label="Pancreatic juice\n~0.8-1.5 L/d\n(HCO3− rich)"];
        S_JEJSEC   [label="Jejunal crypt secretion\n(CFTR, Cl− driven)"];
        S_TOTSEC   [label="Total secretory input SEC\n≈ 4-6 L/d", shape=octagon, fillcolor="#f6e3a0", color="#a08000"];
        S_ACIDINAC [label="Acid inactivates pancreatic\nlipase & deconjugates bile\n→ steatorrhoea", fillcolor="#f5d9d9", color="#a04040"];

        S_SALIVA -> S_TOTSEC; S_GASTRIC -> S_TOTSEC; S_BILE -> S_TOTSEC;
        S_PANC -> S_TOTSEC; S_JEJSEC -> S_TOTSEC;
        S_HYPERSEC -> S_GASTRIC [label="x2-3\nfirst 6-12 mo"];
        S_HYPERSEC -> S_ACIDINAC;
        S_ACIDINAC -> C_FRACFAT [arrowhead=odiamond, color="#b03030"];
        A_STOMACH -> S_GASTRIC;
    }

    /* ============================================================
       CLUSTER 5 — JEJUNAL Na/WATER FLUX: THE SIGN CHANGE
       ============================================================ */
    subgraph cluster_JEJ {
        label=<<B>5. Jejunal Na⁺/water flux — WHERE THE SIGN CHANGES</B><BR/><FONT POINT-SIZE="8">net Na absorption = 0 at luminal [Na⁺] ≈ 90-100 mmol/L; NEGATIVE below it</FONT>>;
        style="filled"; fillcolor="#eef6fb"; color="#2f6f9f"; fontsize=11;
        node [shape=ellipse, fillcolor="#d3e7f5", color="#2f6f9f"];

        J_CNA      [label="Luminal sodium concentration\n[Na]lum", fillcolor="#b9d8ee"];
        J_CEQ      [label="Equivalence concentration [Na]eq ≈ 90-100 mmol/L\nzero-flux set point\n(Fordtran perfusion studies)", shape=octagon, fillcolor="#f6e3a0", color="#a08000"];
        J_JNA      [label="Net Na⁺ flux JNa ∝ ([Na]lum − [Na]eq)\n→ SECRETION when hypotonic", fillcolor="#b9d8ee"];
        J_SGLT1    [label="SGLT1 glucose-coupled Na⁺ uptake\n(1 glucose : 2 Na⁺)", shape=ellipse, fillcolor="#dcecdc", color="#4a7a4a"];
        J_NHE3     [label="NHE3 Na⁺/H⁺ exchanger\nelectroneutral Na absorption"];
        J_PARAC    [label="Paracellular route (claudin-2/15)\nwater & Na flux\n— jejunum is the LEAKIEST gut"];
        J_OSM      [label="Luminal osmolality\n(hyperosmolar feed → secretion)"];
        J_H2OFOLLOW[label="Water follows solute\n(AQP, paracellular drag)"];
        J_WATERTRAP[label="DRINKING PLAIN WATER\n→ [Na]lum ↓ → JNa NEGATIVE\n→ Na⁺ AND volume LOST", shape=doubleoctagon, fillcolor="#f3c9c9", color="#8b1a1a", penwidth=2];
        J_ORSFIX   [label="Glucose-electrolyte solution (ORS)\nORS Na⁺ ≈ 90-120 mmol/L\n+ glucose → SGLT1\n→ JNa POSITIVE", shape=doubleoctagon, fillcolor="#cfe8cf", color="#1a6b1a", penwidth=2];
        J_NETH2O   [label="Net jejunal water absorption\n(or secretion)", fillcolor="#b9d8ee"];

        J_CNA -> J_JNA; J_CEQ -> J_JNA;
        J_SGLT1 -> J_JNA [label="+", color="#2f7f2f"];
        J_NHE3 -> J_JNA [label="+", color="#2f7f2f"];
        J_JNA -> J_H2OFOLLOW -> J_NETH2O;
        J_PARAC -> J_NETH2O; J_OSM -> J_NETH2O [arrowhead=odiamond, color="#b03030"];
        J_WATERTRAP -> J_CNA [label="dilutes", color="#b03030"];
        J_ORSFIX -> J_CNA [label="raises to ~90", color="#2f7f2f"];
        J_ORSFIX -> J_SGLT1 [label="glucose\nsubstrate", color="#2f7f2f"];
        C_FRACNA -> J_JNA [style=dashed];
        S_TOTSEC -> J_CNA [label="secretions are\nisotonic (~140)", style=dashed];
    }

    /* ============================================================
       CLUSTER 6 — COLON AS A DIGESTIVE ORGAN
       ============================================================ */
    subgraph cluster_COLON {
        label=<<B>6. The colon as a digestive organ</B><BR/><FONT POINT-SIZE="8">3-4 L water, 400-800 mmol Na⁺, and up to ~1000 kcal/day of SCFA salvage</FONT>>;
        style="filled"; fillcolor="#f3f0f8"; color="#6a4a95"; fontsize=11;
        node [shape=ellipse, fillcolor="#e2dbf0", color="#6a4a95"];

        K_CAP      [label="Colonic water capacity\n≈ 3-4 L/d x COLONFRAC", fillcolor="#cfc4e6"];
        K_ENAC     [label="ENaC (aldosterone-driven)\n→ near-complete Na⁺ recovery"];
        K_ALDO     [label="Aldosterone (volume depletion →\nRAAS → colonic Na avidity)", shape=ellipse, fillcolor="#dcecdc", color="#4a7a4a"];
        K_FERMENT  [label="Bacterial fermentation of\nunabsorbed carbohydrate & fibre"];
        K_SCFA     [label="Short-chain fatty acids SCFA\nacetate·propionate·butyrate\n~1.5-2 kcal per g CHO fermented", fillcolor="#cfc4e6"];
        K_SCFAKCAL [label="Colonic energy salvage\nup to ~1000 kcal/d\n(Nordgaard)", shape=octagon, fillcolor="#f6e3a0", color="#a08000"];
        K_BUTYRATE [label="Butyrate → colonocyte fuel\n+ mucosal trophic support · barrier strengthening", shape=ellipse, fillcolor="#dcecdc", color="#4a7a4a"];
        K_SCFANA   [label="SCFA-stimulated Na absorption"];
        K_MICROAD  [label="Fermentative capacity adapts\nover months (microbiome shift)", shape=ellipse, fillcolor="#dcecdc", color="#4a7a4a"];
        K_TRANSIT  [label="Colonic transit\n(long → more salvage)"];
        K_NOCOLON  [label="END-JEJUNOSTOMY:\nzero water, zero Na, zero SCFA salvage\n→ 3x higher PN requirement", shape=doubleoctagon, fillcolor="#f3c9c9", color="#8b1a1a", penwidth=2];

        A_COLON -> K_CAP; A_COLON -> K_FERMENT;
        K_ALDO -> K_ENAC -> K_CAP;
        K_FERMENT -> K_SCFA -> K_SCFAKCAL;
        K_SCFA -> K_BUTYRATE; K_SCFA -> K_SCFANA -> K_CAP;
        K_MICROAD -> K_FERMENT; K_TRANSIT -> K_FERMENT;
        A_COLON -> K_NOCOLON [label="COLONFRAC = 0", style=dashed, color="#b03030"];
        K_NOCOLON -> K_CAP [arrowhead=odiamond, color="#8b1a1a", penwidth=1.6];
        K_NOCOLON -> K_SCFAKCAL [arrowhead=odiamond, color="#8b1a1a", penwidth=1.6];
    }

    /* ============================================================
       CLUSTER 7 — L-CELL / ENTEROHORMONAL AXIS (the broken loop)
       ============================================================ */
    subgraph cluster_LCELL {
        label=<<B>7. L-cell enterohormonal axis — THE BROKEN LOOP</B><BR/><FONT POINT-SIZE="8">L-cells live in distal ileum &amp; proximal colon — exactly the tissue that is resected</FONT>>;
        style="filled"; fillcolor="#fffbe8"; color="#8a7000"; fontsize=11;
        node [shape=ellipse, fillcolor="#faf0c0", color="#8a7000"];

        L_MASS     [label="L-cell mass\n∝ remnant ileum + colon", fillcolor="#f3e49a"];
        L_NUTSENS  [label="Luminal nutrient sensing\n(FFAR2/3, GPR119, SGLT1)"];
        L_PROGLU   [label="Proglucagon gene\n→ PC1/3 cleavage"];
        L_GLP2     [label="Endogenous GLP-2 (1-33)\npostprandial surge", fillcolor="#f3e49a"];
        L_GLP1     [label="GLP-1\n(gastric emptying ↓, satiety)"];
        L_PYY      [label="PYY 3-36\n(ileal brake, transit ↓)"];
        L_NEUROT   [label="Neurotensin"];
        L_DPP4     [label="DPP-4\ncleaves GLP-2 at Ala2-Gly3\n→ native t½ ≈ 7 min", shape=ellipse, fillcolor="#f5d9d9", color="#a04040"];
        L_GLP2R    [label="GLP2R (expressed on subepithelial\nmyofibroblasts and enteric neurons,\nnot on the epithelium)\nGLP-2 receptor — INDIRECT action"];
        L_IGF1LOC  [label="Local IGF-1 · KGF · ErbB ligands\nfrom subepithelial myofibroblasts\n= the actual mitogen", shape=ellipse, fillcolor="#dcecdc", color="#4a7a4a"];
        L_ENS      [label="Enteric NO/VIP pathway\nENS relay → blood flow ↑,\nmotility ↓"];
        L_BLUNTED  [label="BLUNTED postprandial GLP-2/PYY\nin SBS with resected ileum", fillcolor="#f5d9d9", color="#a04040"];
        L_GHRELIN  [label="Ghrelin ↑\n(hyperphagia drive)"];
        L_GASTRIN  [label="Gastrin ↑\n(loss of inhibitory peptides)", fillcolor="#f5d9d9", color="#a04040"];
        L_CCK      [label="CCK\n(gallbladder contraction)"];

        A_ILEUM -> L_MASS; A_COLON -> L_MASS;
        L_NUTSENS -> L_PROGLU; L_MASS -> L_PROGLU;
        L_PROGLU -> L_GLP2; L_PROGLU -> L_GLP1; L_MASS -> L_PYY; L_MASS -> L_NEUROT;
        L_DPP4 -> L_GLP2 [arrowhead=odiamond, label="t½ 7 min", color="#b03030"];
        L_GLP2 -> L_GLP2R -> L_IGF1LOC;
        L_GLP2R -> L_ENS;
        L_MASS -> L_BLUNTED [label="mass ↓ →", style=dashed, color="#b03030"];
        L_BLUNTED -> L_GLP2 [arrowhead=odiamond, color="#b03030"];
        L_GASTRIN -> S_HYPERSEC;
        L_CCK -> S_BILE;
    }

    /* ============================================================
       CLUSTER 8 — MOTILITY / TRANSIT / THE ILEAL BRAKE
       ============================================================ */
    subgraph cluster_MOT {
        label=<<B>8. Motility, transit and the ileal brake</B><BR/><FONT POINT-SIZE="8">contact time is a multiplicand in the Damköhler product — this is why transit drugs work</FONT>>;
        style="filled"; fillcolor="#f6f2ec"; color="#7a5a3a"; fontsize=11;
        node [shape=ellipse, fillcolor="#eadfd0", color="#7a5a3a"];

        M_GE       [label="Gastric emptying rate"];
        M_BRAKE    [label="ILEAL BRAKE\n(GLP-1 + PYY + neurotensin)", fillcolor="#dcd0bd"];
        M_TRANSIT  [label="Small-bowel transit time SBTT\n(normal 3-4 h; SBS <1 h)", fillcolor="#dcd0bd"];
        M_MMC      [label="Migrating motor complex MMC\n(bacterial clearance)"];
        M_ICVLOSS  [label="ICV loss → colonic reflux,\nfaster emptying, SIBO", fillcolor="#f5d9d9", color="#a04040"];
        M_MU       [label="Enteric μ-opioid receptors\n→ transit ↓↓"];
        M_MIXING   [label="Segmental mixing efficiency"];
        M_DILATLOOP[label="Stasis in dilated loop\n→ SIBO, not absorption", fillcolor="#f5d9d9", color="#a04040"];

        L_GLP1 -> M_BRAKE; L_PYY -> M_BRAKE; L_NEUROT -> M_BRAKE;
        M_BRAKE -> M_GE [arrowhead=odiamond]; M_BRAKE -> M_TRANSIT [label="prolongs", color="#2f7f2f"];
        L_ENS -> M_TRANSIT [label="prolongs", color="#2f7f2f", style=dashed];
        M_TRANSIT -> C_CONTACT; M_MIXING -> C_CONTACT;
        M_ICVLOSS -> M_TRANSIT [arrowhead=odiamond, color="#b03030"];
        A_ICV -> M_ICVLOSS [style=dashed];
        M_MU -> M_TRANSIT [label="prolongs", color="#2f7f2f"];
        A_DILAT -> M_DILATLOOP; M_MMC -> M_DILATLOOP [arrowhead=odiamond];
        M_GE -> J_OSM [label="rapid delivery →\nhyperosmolar jejunum", style=dashed];
    }

    /* ============================================================
       CLUSTER 9 — STRUCTURAL ADAPTATION
       ============================================================ */
    subgraph cluster_ADAPT {
        label=<<B>9. Structural adaptation (weeks → 2 years)</B><BR/><FONT POINT-SIZE="8">NUTRIENT-GATED: the trophic signal is a PRODUCT of luminal nutrient x GLP2R occupancy</FONT>>;
        style="filled"; fillcolor="#eef7ee"; color="#3f7a3f"; fontsize=11;
        node [shape=ellipse, fillcolor="#d5ebd5", color="#3f7a3f"];

        D_LUMNUT   [label="Luminal nutrient exposure\n(enteral feeding)", fillcolor="#bfe0bf"];
        D_TROPHIC  [label="TROPHIC SIGNAL = luminal nutrient x GLP2R occupancy\n= a PRODUCT\n(zero enteral feed → zero adaptation)", shape=octagon, fillcolor="#f6e3a0", color="#a08000"];
        D_CRYPT    [label="Crypt cell proliferation\n(Ki-67, Lgr5+ ISC)"];
        D_VILLUS   [label="Villus height\n(+30-50% achievable)", fillcolor="#bfe0bf"];
        D_CRYPTD   [label="Crypt depth"];
        D_MUCMASS  [label="Mucosal absorptive mass", fillcolor="#bfe0bf"];
        D_APOPT    [label="Reduced enterocyte apoptosis"];
        D_DILATION [label="Luminal dilation (compensatory)\n(surface ↑ but stasis ↑)"];
        D_LENGTHEN [label="Lengthening — meaningful\nonly in the growing child"];
        D_TIMECOURSE[label="Adaptation time constant\nτ ≈ 6-12 months,\nplateau by ~2 years", shape=box, fillcolor="#dbe7f3", color="#5b7fa6"];
        D_IGF1SYS  [label="Systemic IGF-1 (GH-driven)"];
        D_EGF      [label="EGF from salivary and\nBrunner glands"];
        D_GLUT     [label="Glutamine — the enterocyte's\nprincipal fuel"];
        D_POLYAM   [label="Polyamines (ODC) — obligatory\nfor crypt mitosis"];
        D_NPO      [label="NIL BY MOUTH on full PN\n→ villus atrophy, NO adaptation,\nand NO GLP-2 analogue response", shape=doubleoctagon, fillcolor="#f3c9c9", color="#8b1a1a", penwidth=2];

        D_LUMNUT -> D_TROPHIC; L_IGF1LOC -> D_TROPHIC;
        D_TROPHIC -> D_CRYPT -> D_VILLUS; D_CRYPT -> D_CRYPTD;
        D_TROPHIC -> D_APOPT [arrowhead=odiamond];
        D_VILLUS -> D_MUCMASS; D_CRYPTD -> D_MUCMASS; A_SBL -> D_MUCMASS;
        D_MUCMASS -> A_SURFACE; D_DILATION -> A_SURFACE;
        D_DILATION -> A_DILAT [style=dashed, color="#b03030"];
        D_LENGTHEN -> A_SBL [style=dashed];
        D_TIMECOURSE -> D_VILLUS [style=dashed];
        D_IGF1SYS -> D_CRYPT; D_EGF -> D_CRYPT; D_GLUT -> D_CRYPT;
        D_POLYAM -> D_CRYPT;
        D_NPO -> D_LUMNUT [arrowhead=odiamond, color="#8b1a1a", penwidth=1.6];
        D_NPO -> D_TROPHIC [arrowhead=odiamond, color="#8b1a1a", penwidth=1.6, label="PRODUCT → 0"];
        D_LUMNUT -> L_NUTSENS [label="also drives\nL-cell secretion", style=dashed, color="#2f7f2f"];
    }

    /* ============================================================
       CLUSTER 10 — FUNCTIONAL ADAPTATION
       ============================================================ */
    subgraph cluster_FUNC {
        label=<<B>10. Functional adaptation</B><BR/><FONT POINT-SIZE="8">per-area transport capacity rises even when villus height does not</FONT>>;
        style="filled"; fillcolor="#f0f7f4"; color="#3f7a6a"; fontsize=11;
        node [shape=ellipse, fillcolor="#d5ebe4", color="#3f7a6a"];

        F_SGLT1UP  [label="SGLT1 upregulation\ndensity ↑"];
        F_NHE3UP   [label="NHE3 upregulation\ndensity ↑"];
        F_PEPT1    [label="PEPT1 peptide transporter\ndi/tripeptide uptake ↑"];
        F_BBENZ    [label="Brush-border enzymes\n(lactase, sucrase-isomaltase)"];
        F_FABP     [label="FABP · fat re-esterification\nfatty acid binding &\nchylomicron assembly"];
        F_ZO       [label="Tight-junction remodelling\n(claudin switch)"];
        F_KAPPAUP  [label="Effective per-area constant k ↑", fillcolor="#bfdfd4"];
        F_CAAB     [label="Active Ca²⁺ absorption (TRPV6,\nactive vitamin D dependent)"];
        F_MGAB     [label="Mg²⁺ absorption (TRPM6/7, mainly ileum)\n— ileum-dependent"];

        D_TROPHIC -> F_SGLT1UP; D_TROPHIC -> F_NHE3UP; D_TROPHIC -> F_PEPT1;
        D_TROPHIC -> F_BBENZ; D_TROPHIC -> F_FABP; D_TROPHIC -> F_ZO;
        F_SGLT1UP -> J_SGLT1; F_NHE3UP -> J_NHE3;
        F_SGLT1UP -> F_KAPPAUP; F_NHE3UP -> F_KAPPAUP; F_PEPT1 -> F_KAPPAUP;
        F_BBENZ -> F_KAPPAUP; F_FABP -> F_KAPPAUP;
        F_KAPPAUP -> C_KAPPA;
        A_ILEUM -> F_MGAB [label="site-specific", style=dashed];
    }

    /* ============================================================
       CLUSTER 11 — BILE ACID ENTEROHEPATIC CIRCULATION
       ============================================================ */
    subgraph cluster_BILE {
        label=<<B>11. Bile acid enterohepatic circulation</B><BR/><FONT POINT-SIZE="8">the 100 cm rule: below it, bile-acid diarrhoea; above it, pool depletion and steatorrhoea — OPPOSITE therapies</FONT>>;
        style="filled"; fillcolor="#fdf6e8"; color="#8a6a20"; fontsize=11;
        node [shape=ellipse, fillcolor="#f6ead0", color="#8a6a20"];

        B_SYNTH    [label="Hepatic BA synthesis (CYP7A1)"];
        B_POOL     [label="Bile acid pool size (~3-4 g)", fillcolor="#eeda9f"];
        B_ASBT     [label="ASBT (terminal ileum)\nileal Na-dependent BA transporter\n— 95% reclaimed HERE"];
        B_FGF19    [label="FGF19 from ileal FXR\n→ feedback inhibition of CYP7A1"];
        B_MICELLE  [label="Micellar solubilisation\n(critical micellar conc.)"];
        B_LOSS     [label="BA spill into colon"];
        B_BAD      [label="BILE ACID DIARRHOEA (resection <100 cm)\ncolonic secretory drive", fillcolor="#f5d9d9", color="#a04040"];
        B_DEPLETE  [label="POOL DEPLETION (resection >100 cm)\n→ micelles fail\n→ FAT malabsorption", fillcolor="#f5d9d9", color="#a04040"];
        B_100CM    [label="THE 100 cm RULE\n<100 cm ileum resected → BAD\n>100 cm → steatorrhoea", shape=octagon, fillcolor="#f6e3a0", color="#a08000"];
        B_LITHO    [label="Cholelithiasis\n(stasis + BA loss + no CCK)", fillcolor="#f5d9d9", color="#a04040"];
        B_SEQTRAP  [label="CHOLESTYRAMINE REVERSES SIGN:\nhelps at <100 cm,\nWORSENS steatorrhoea at >100 cm", shape=doubleoctagon, fillcolor="#f3c9c9", color="#8b1a1a", penwidth=2];

        B_SYNTH -> B_POOL -> B_MICELLE -> C_FRACFAT;
        B_POOL -> B_ASBT -> B_POOL [label="recycle 6-10x/d"];
        B_ASBT -> B_FGF19 -> B_SYNTH [arrowhead=odiamond, style=dashed];
        A_ILEUM -> B_ASBT; B_ASBT -> B_LOSS [arrowhead=odiamond];
        B_LOSS -> B_BAD; B_LOSS -> B_DEPLETE [label="if synthesis\ncannot keep up"];
        B_100CM -> B_BAD; B_100CM -> B_DEPLETE;
        B_DEPLETE -> B_MICELLE [arrowhead=odiamond, color="#b03030"];
        B_BAD -> K_CAP [arrowhead=odiamond, color="#b03030", label="secretory"];
        B_POOL -> B_LITHO [arrowhead=odiamond]; L_CCK -> B_LITHO [arrowhead=odiamond];
        B_SEQTRAP -> B_POOL [arrowhead=odiamond, color="#8b1a1a"];
    }

    /* ============================================================
       CLUSTER 12 — SIBO / MICROBIOME / D-LACTATE
       ============================================================ */
    subgraph cluster_MICRO {
        label=<<B>12. SIBO, microbiome and D-lactic acidosis</B><BR/><FONT POINT-SIZE="8">D-lactic encephalopathy REQUIRES a colon — it cannot occur in end-jejunostomy</FONT>>;
        style="filled"; fillcolor="#f8f0f4"; color="#8a3a5a"; fontsize=11;
        node [shape=ellipse, fillcolor="#f0dbe4", color="#8a3a5a"];

        G_SIBO     [label="Small intestinal bacterial\novergrowth SIBO (~60-70% of SBS)", fillcolor="#e4c3d1"];
        G_ICVGONE  [label="ICV loss → retrograde colonisation"];
        G_STASIS   [label="Stasis in a dilated,\nslow-transit segment"];
        G_ACIDGONE [label="Acid suppression (PPI) removes\nthe gastric bacterial filter", fillcolor="#f5d9d9", color="#a04040"];
        G_DECONJ   [label="Bacterial BA deconjugation\n→ micelles fail"];
        G_MUCINJ   [label="Bacterial mucosal injury,\nvillus blunting"];
        G_B12CONS  [label="Bacterial B12 consumption"];
        G_DLACT    [label="D-lactate (Lactobacillus) from\ncolonic carbohydrate overload", fillcolor="#e4c3d1"];
        G_ENCEPH   [label="D-lactic acidosis · encephalopathy:\nataxia, slurred speech,\nanion-gap acidosis", shape=diamond, fillcolor="#e6d0ea", color="#6a3a8a"];
        G_DYSBIOS  [label="Proteobacteria-dominant dysbiosis\nLactobacillus-dominant dysbiosis"];
        G_ENDOTOX  [label="Intestinal permeability ↑ → endotoxin\ntranslocation to the portal vein"];
        G_NEEDCOL  [label="D-LACTIC ACIDOSIS REQUIRES A COLON\n— structural null in end-jejunostomy", shape=doubleoctagon, fillcolor="#cfe8cf", color="#1a6b1a", penwidth=2];

        G_ICVGONE -> G_SIBO; G_STASIS -> G_SIBO; G_ACIDGONE -> G_SIBO;
        M_ICVLOSS -> G_ICVGONE; M_DILATLOOP -> G_STASIS;
        G_SIBO -> G_DECONJ -> B_MICELLE [arrowhead=odiamond, color="#b03030"];
        G_SIBO -> G_MUCINJ -> D_VILLUS [arrowhead=odiamond, color="#b03030"];
        G_SIBO -> G_B12CONS; G_SIBO -> G_DYSBIOS -> G_DLACT;
        K_FERMENT -> G_DLACT [label="CHO overload"];
        G_DLACT -> G_ENCEPH;
        G_NEEDCOL -> G_DLACT [style=dashed, color="#1a6b1a"];
        G_SIBO -> G_ENDOTOX;
    }

    /* ============================================================
       CLUSTER 13 — ENERGY BALANCE
       ============================================================ */
    subgraph cluster_NRG {
        label=<<B>13. The ENERGY conservation equation</B><BR/><FONT POINT-SIZE="8">absorbed − expended = deficit → PN calories</FONT>>;
        style="filled"; fillcolor="#fffbf0"; color="#8a7020"; fontsize=11;
        node [shape=ellipse, fillcolor="#f7edcf", color="#8a7020"];

        N_ORALKCAL [label="Oral energy intake"];
        N_HYPERPH  [label="Compensatory hyperphagia\nspontaneous, up to\n1.5-2 x normal intake", shape=ellipse, fillcolor="#dcecdc", color="#4a7a4a"];
        N_ABSKCAL  [label="Absorbed energy\n= oral x coefficient"];
        N_FECALKCAL[label="Faecal energy loss\n(often 40-60% of intake)", fillcolor="#f5d9d9", color="#a04040"];
        N_STEAT    [label="Steatorrhoea\n(fat is the dominant loss)", fillcolor="#f5d9d9", color="#a04040"];
        N_REE      [label="Resting energy expenditure REE\n(∝ lean mass)"];
        N_TEE      [label="Total energy expenditure TEE\n= REE x activity"];
        N_NRGBAL   [label="ENERGY BALANCE\n= absorbed + SCFA − TEE", shape=octagon, fillcolor="#f6e3a0", color="#a08000"];
        N_LEAN     [label="Lean body mass"];
        N_FAT      [label="Fat mass"];
        N_WEIGHT   [label="Body weight", shape=diamond, fillcolor="#e6d0ea", color="#6a3a8a"];
        N_SARCO    [label="Sarcopenia, weakness", fillcolor="#f5d9d9", color="#a04040"];

        N_HYPERPH -> N_ORALKCAL; N_ORALKCAL -> N_ABSKCAL;
        C_FRACCHO -> N_ABSKCAL; C_FRACFAT -> N_ABSKCAL; C_FRACPRO -> N_ABSKCAL;
        N_ORALKCAL -> N_FECALKCAL; C_FRACFAT -> N_STEAT [arrowhead=odiamond];
        N_STEAT -> N_FECALKCAL;
        N_ABSKCAL -> N_NRGBAL; K_SCFAKCAL -> N_NRGBAL;
        N_TEE -> N_NRGBAL [arrowhead=odiamond];
        N_REE -> N_TEE; N_LEAN -> N_REE;
        N_NRGBAL -> N_LEAN; N_NRGBAL -> N_FAT;
        N_LEAN -> N_WEIGHT; N_FAT -> N_WEIGHT;
        N_LEAN -> N_SARCO [arrowhead=odiamond];
        D_LUMNUT -> N_ORALKCAL [dir=back, style=dashed];
    }

    /* ============================================================
       CLUSTER 14 — FLUID BALANCE
       ============================================================ */
    subgraph cluster_BAL {
        label=<<B>14. The FLUID and SODIUM conservation equation</B><BR/><FONT POINT-SIZE="8">this is the equation whose residual the central line fills</FONT>>;
        style="filled"; fillcolor="#eef8fb"; color="#20708a"; fontsize=11;
        node [shape=ellipse, fillcolor="#d0ebf2", color="#20708a"];

        W_ORAL     [label="Oral fluid intake"];
        W_DELIV    [label="Water delivered to the jejunum\n= oral + secretions"];
        W_JEJABS   [label="Jejunal net absorption\n(or secretion)"];
        W_COLABS   [label="Colonic salvage"];
        W_OUTPUT   [label="Stool / stoma output (L/d)\n— the measurable", fillcolor="#a8d8e6"];
        W_INSENS   [label="Insensible loss ~0.5-0.8 L/d"];
        W_URINE    [label="24-h urine output\n— THE WEANING SIGNAL", fillcolor="#a8d8e6"];
        W_FLUIDBAL [label="FLUID BALANCE\n= absorbed + PN − output − insensible", shape=octagon, fillcolor="#f6e3a0", color="#a08000"];
        W_NABAL    [label="SODIUM balance\n(stoma Na ≈ 90-100 mmol/L)", shape=octagon, fillcolor="#f6e3a0", color="#a08000"];
        W_TBW      [label="Total body water /\neffective circulating volume", fillcolor="#a8d8e6"];
        W_DEHYD    [label="Chronic volume depletion", fillcolor="#f5d9d9", color="#a04040"];
        W_RAAS     [label="RAAS activation\nrenin-angiotensin-aldosterone"];
        W_UNA      [label="Urinary Na⁺ <10 mmol/L\n— the earliest, cheapest\ndepletion marker", shape=diamond, fillcolor="#e6d0ea", color="#6a3a8a"];

        W_ORAL -> W_DELIV; S_TOTSEC -> W_DELIV;
        W_DELIV -> W_JEJABS; J_NETH2O -> W_JEJABS;
        W_DELIV -> W_COLABS; K_CAP -> W_COLABS;
        W_DELIV -> W_OUTPUT; W_JEJABS -> W_OUTPUT [arrowhead=odiamond];
        W_COLABS -> W_OUTPUT [arrowhead=odiamond];
        W_JEJABS -> W_FLUIDBAL; W_COLABS -> W_FLUIDBAL;
        W_OUTPUT -> W_FLUIDBAL [arrowhead=odiamond]; W_INSENS -> W_FLUIDBAL [arrowhead=odiamond];
        W_FLUIDBAL -> W_TBW; W_FLUIDBAL -> W_URINE;
        J_JNA -> W_NABAL; K_ENAC -> W_NABAL; W_OUTPUT -> W_NABAL [arrowhead=odiamond];
        W_TBW -> W_DEHYD [arrowhead=odiamond]; W_DEHYD -> W_RAAS -> K_ALDO;
        W_DEHYD -> W_UNA; W_RAAS -> W_UNA;
    }

    /* ============================================================
       CLUSTER 15 — PN PRESCRIPTION AS A CLOSED-LOOP CONTROLLER
       ============================================================ */
    subgraph cluster_PN {
        label=<<B>15. PN prescription as a CLOSED-LOOP CONTROLLER</B><BR/><FONT POINT-SIZE="8">the STEPS weaning algorithm: cut PN when 24-h urine rises ≥10% above baseline</FONT>>;
        style="filled"; fillcolor="#fff2e8"; color="#a04a10"; fontsize=11;
        node [shape=hexagon, fillcolor="#fbd9bf", color="#a04a10"];

        P_DEFICIT  [label="Computed deficit\n(fluid L/d, energy kcal/d)", shape=octagon, fillcolor="#f6e3a0", color="#a08000"];
        P_PNVOL    [label="PRESCRIBED PN VOLUME\n(L/week) — an OUTPUT", fillcolor="#f7c49a"];
        P_PNKCAL   [label="PN energy (kcal/d)"];
        P_PNNA     [label="PN sodium, K, Mg, PO4"];
        P_ILE      [label="Lipid emulsion choice:\nsoybean / MCT-LCT / SMOF /\nfish-oil (Omegaven)", fillcolor="#f7c49a"];
        P_DAYSWK   [label="PN infusion days/week\n(cycling → 1-2 nights off)"];
        P_URINETRG [label="URINE-OUTPUT TRIGGER:\nurine ≥ 1.10 x baseline\n→ reduce PN", shape=octagon, fillcolor="#f6e3a0", color="#a08000"];
        P_WEIGHTG  [label="Weight & electrolyte guardrails\n(block reduction if losing weight)"];
        P_TAPER    [label="Taper step\n(−10 to −20% volume,\nthen drop a day)"];
        P_HYDRSAFE [label="Re-escalate if urine falls /\nUNa <10 / weight drops"];
        P_PLACEBOART[label="THE PLACEBO ARM RESPONSE:\nany patient with unused absorptive\nreserve is weaned BY THE ALGORITHM,\ndrug or no drug", shape=doubleoctagon, fillcolor="#f3c9c9", color="#8b1a1a", penwidth=2];

        W_FLUIDBAL -> P_DEFICIT; N_NRGBAL -> P_DEFICIT;
        P_DEFICIT -> P_PNVOL; P_DEFICIT -> P_PNKCAL; P_DEFICIT -> P_PNNA;
        W_URINE -> P_URINETRG [style=dotted, penwidth=1.4];
        P_URINETRG -> P_TAPER; P_WEIGHTG -> P_TAPER [arrowhead=odiamond];
        P_TAPER -> P_PNVOL [arrowhead=odiamond, color="#2f7f2f", penwidth=1.5];
        P_TAPER -> P_DAYSWK;
        P_HYDRSAFE -> P_PNVOL [color="#b03030"];
        W_UNA -> P_HYDRSAFE [style=dotted]; N_WEIGHT -> P_WEIGHTG [style=dotted];
        P_PNVOL -> W_FLUIDBAL [label="closes the loop", color="#2f7f2f", penwidth=1.5];
        P_PNKCAL -> N_NRGBAL [color="#2f7f2f"];
        P_URINETRG -> P_PLACEBOART [style=dashed, color="#8b1a1a"];
    }

    /* ============================================================
       CLUSTER 16 — GLP-2 ANALOGUE PHARMACOLOGY
       ============================================================ */
    subgraph cluster_GLP2PK {
        label=<<B>16. GLP-2 analogue pharmacology</B><BR/><FONT POINT-SIZE="8">one substitution (Ala2→Gly) buys a 20-fold half-life; that substitution IS the drug</FONT>>;
        style="filled"; fillcolor="#fff0f5"; color="#a01050"; fontsize=11;
        node [shape=hexagon, fillcolor="#fbc9dd", color="#a01050"];

        T_TEDSC    [label="TEDUGLUTIDE 0.05 mg/kg/day SC\n[Gly2]-GLP-2, DPP-4 resistant", fillcolor="#f7a8c6"];
        T_TEDPK    [label="Teduglutide PK\nF ≈ 88%, Tmax 3-5 h,\nt½ ≈ 2 h, Vd/F ≈ 26 L", shape=ellipse, fillcolor="#f2dbe4", color="#a01050"];
        T_APRA     [label="APRAGLUTIDE weekly SC\n(albumin-binding, t½ ~30 h)"];
        T_GLEPA    [label="GLEPAGLUTIDE weekly/2x-weekly SC"];
        T_NATIVE   [label="NATIVE GLP-2 infusion\nt½ 7 min — structural null:\nno sustained mucosal effect", shape=doubleoctagon, fillcolor="#f3c9c9", color="#8b1a1a", penwidth=2];
        T_OCC      [label="GLP2R occupancy\n(Emax / EC50)", shape=ellipse, fillcolor="#f2dbe4", color="#a01050"];
        T_TURNOVER [label="Mucosal PD turnover\nτ ≈ 3-6 weeks ≫ drug t½\n→ once-daily works despite t½ 2 h", shape=octagon, fillcolor="#f6e3a0", color="#a08000"];
        T_ADA      [label="Anti-drug antibodies (ADA ~30-40%) —\nmostly non-neutralising"];
        T_CITRISE  [label="Plasma citrulline ↑\n(enterocyte mass biomarker)", shape=ellipse, fillcolor="#dcecdc", color="#4a7a4a"];
        T_FLUIDOL  [label="Fluid overload / oedema\n(absorption improves faster\nthan PN is cut)", shape=ellipse, fillcolor="#f5d9d9", color="#a04040"];
        T_POLYP    [label="Colorectal polyp growth —\nmandated colonoscopy surveillance", shape=ellipse, fillcolor="#f5d9d9", color="#a04040"];
        T_STOMAENL [label="Stoma oedema and enlargement,\nabdominal distension"];
        T_BILIARY  [label="Biliary and pancreatic events\n(surveillance required)", shape=ellipse, fillcolor="#f5d9d9", color="#a04040"];
        T_GATED    [label="EFFECT IS GATED BY LUMINAL NUTRIENT\n(product, not sum)", shape=doubleoctagon, fillcolor="#cfe8cf", color="#1a6b1a", penwidth=2];

        T_TEDSC -> T_TEDPK -> T_OCC; T_APRA -> T_OCC; T_GLEPA -> T_OCC;
        T_NATIVE -> T_OCC [label="transient only", style=dashed, color="#8b1a1a"];
        L_DPP4 -> T_NATIVE [label="cleaves", color="#b03030"];
        L_DPP4 -> T_TEDPK [arrowhead=odiamond, style=dashed, label="resistant"];
        T_OCC -> L_GLP2R; T_OCC -> T_TURNOVER -> D_TROPHIC [color="#2f7f2f", penwidth=1.5];
        T_ADA -> T_OCC [arrowhead=odiamond, style=dashed];
        D_MUCMASS -> T_CITRISE;
        T_OCC -> T_FLUIDOL; T_OCC -> T_POLYP; T_OCC -> T_STOMAENL; T_OCC -> T_BILIARY;
        T_GATED -> T_TURNOVER [arrowhead=odiamond, color="#1a6b1a"];
        D_LUMNUT -> T_GATED [style=dashed, color="#1a6b1a"];
    }

    /* ============================================================
       CLUSTER 17 — ADJUNCTIVE PHARMACOTHERAPY
       ============================================================ */
    subgraph cluster_DRUG {
        label=<<B>17. Adjunctive pharmacotherapy</B><BR/><FONT POINT-SIZE="8">each drug changes ONE term of the balance — and two of them change it the wrong way</FONT>>;
        style="filled"; fillcolor="#fdf0e0"; color="#8a5a10"; fontsize=11;
        node [shape=hexagon, fillcolor="#f8dfb8", color="#8a5a10"];

        R_LOP      [label="LOPERAMIDE 4-16 mg/d\n(μ-agonist,\nP-gp limited CNS entry)"];
        R_COD      [label="CODEINE phosphate 30-60 mg"];
        R_OPIUM    [label="Tincture of opium\n(refractory high output)"];
        R_PPI      [label="High-dose PPI / H2 blocker\n→ gastric secretion ↓ 1-2 L/d"];
        R_OCT      [label="OCTREOTIDE SC/LAR — output ↓\nBUT suppresses IGF-1 and\nMAY IMPAIR ADAPTATION", fillcolor="#f5c9a0"];
        R_GH       [label="Somatropin 0.1 mg/kg/d x 4 weeks\nrhGH (Zorbtive) + glutamine\n— modest, transient"];
        R_CHOL     [label="CHOLESTYRAMINE 4 g"];
        R_RIFAX    [label="RIFAXIMIN 550 mg bid (SIBO)"];
        R_ORS      [label="Oral rehydration solution\nORS (Na 90-120 mmol/L\n+ glucose)", fillcolor="#c9e8d0"];
        R_CLON     [label="Transdermal CLONIDINE\n(α2, secretion ↓)"];
        R_CHOLINE  [label="Choline / taurine supplementation"];
        R_ABXLOCK  [label="Ethanol / taurolidine\ncatheter lock"];
        R_CITRATE  [label="Potassium citrate,\nlow-oxalate diet, Ca with meals"];
        R_AKI      [label="(context node) Volume-depletion AKI", shape=ellipse, fillcolor="#f5d9d9", color="#a04040"];
        R_OCTTRAP  [label="OCTREOTIDE TRADE-OFF:\noutput ↓ now, adaptation ↓ later\n— net benefit is time-dependent", shape=doubleoctagon, fillcolor="#f3c9c9", color="#8b1a1a", penwidth=2];

        R_LOP -> M_MU; R_COD -> M_MU; R_OPIUM -> M_MU;
        R_PPI -> S_GASTRIC [arrowhead=odiamond, color="#2f7f2f"];
        R_PPI -> G_ACIDGONE [color="#b03030", label="the cost"];
        R_OCT -> S_TOTSEC [arrowhead=odiamond, color="#2f7f2f"];
        R_OCT -> R_OCTTRAP; R_OCTTRAP -> D_IGF1SYS [arrowhead=odiamond, color="#8b1a1a"];
        R_OCT -> M_TRANSIT [label="prolongs"];
        R_GH -> D_IGF1SYS [color="#2f7f2f"]; R_GH -> W_TBW [label="Na retention"];
        R_CHOL -> B_SEQTRAP; R_CHOL -> B_BAD [arrowhead=odiamond, color="#2f7f2f"];
        R_RIFAX -> G_SIBO [arrowhead=odiamond, color="#2f7f2f"];
        R_ORS -> J_ORSFIX [color="#2f7f2f", penwidth=1.5];
        R_CLON -> S_JEJSEC [arrowhead=odiamond];
        R_CITRATE -> R_OXAL [arrowhead=odiamond, color="#2f7f2f"];
        R_GLUTS     [label="Oral glutamine supplementation\n— little effect alone"];
        R_GLUTS -> D_GLUT;
        R_OXAL      [label="(context) Urinary oxalate", shape=ellipse, fillcolor="#f5d9d9", color="#a04040"];
    }

    /* ============================================================
       CLUSTER 18 — IFALD
       ============================================================ */
    subgraph cluster_IFALD {
        label=<<B>18. Intestinal failure-associated liver disease (IFALD)</B><BR/><FONT POINT-SIZE="8">the lipid emulsion is the dose; changing the oil changes the disease</FONT>>;
        style="filled"; fillcolor="#f2f7ea"; color="#5a7a20"; fontsize=11;
        node [shape=ellipse, fillcolor="#e0ecc9", color="#5a7a20"];

        I_PHYTO    [label="PHYTOSTEROL load\n(soybean ILE ~350 µg/mL;\nSMOF lower; fish-oil ≈ 0)", fillcolor="#f5d9d9", color="#a04040"];
        I_FXRANT   [label="Phytosterols antagonise\nhepatic FXR → BSEP ↓", fillcolor="#f5d9d9", color="#a04040"];
        I_CHOLINE  [label="Choline deficiency\n(PN lacks choline)", fillcolor="#f5d9d9", color="#a04040"];
        I_NOENT    [label="Absence of enteral stimulation\n→ biliary stasis, ↓ CCK", fillcolor="#f5d9d9", color="#a04040"];
        I_OVERFEED [label="Glucose / lipid overfeeding\n→ de novo lipogenesis"];
        I_STEATO   [label="Hepatic steatosis"];
        I_CHOLEST  [label="Cholestasis (conjugated\nbilirubin, GGT, ALP ↑)", fillcolor="#f5d9d9", color="#a04040"];
        H_INFLAM   [label="Hepatic inflammation\n(Kupffer, TLR4)"];
        I_FIB      [label="Portal fibrosis → biliary cirrhosis", fillcolor="#f5d9d9", color="#a04040"];
        I_PHTN     [label="Portal hypertension\nsplenomegaly, platelets ↓"];
        I_BILI     [label="Total bilirubin (mg/dL)", shape=diamond, fillcolor="#e6d0ea", color="#6a3a8a"];
        I_FISHOIL  [label="FISH-OIL ILE: phytosterol → 0,\nω3 anti-inflammatory\n→ cholestasis reverses", shape=doubleoctagon, fillcolor="#cfe8cf", color="#1a6b1a", penwidth=2];
        I_LIPIDMIN [label="Lipid minimisation strategy\n(≤1 g/kg/wk)"];
        I_EFAD     [label="Essential fatty acid deficiency\n(the cost of lipid minimisation)", fillcolor="#f5d9d9", color="#a04040"];

        P_ILE -> I_PHYTO; I_PHYTO -> I_FXRANT -> I_CHOLEST;
        I_CHOLINE -> I_STEATO; I_NOENT -> I_CHOLEST; I_OVERFEED -> I_STEATO;
        I_STEATO -> H_INFLAM -> I_FIB; I_CHOLEST -> H_INFLAM;
        I_FIB -> I_PHTN; I_CHOLEST -> I_BILI;
        I_FISHOIL -> I_PHYTO [arrowhead=odiamond, color="#1a6b1a", penwidth=1.6];
        I_FISHOIL -> H_INFLAM [arrowhead=odiamond, color="#1a6b1a"];
        I_LIPIDMIN -> I_PHYTO [arrowhead=odiamond]; I_LIPIDMIN -> I_EFAD [color="#b03030"];
        D_LUMNUT -> I_NOENT [arrowhead=odiamond, color="#2f7f2f"];
        G_ENDOTOX -> H_INFLAM;
    }

    /* ============================================================
       CLUSTER 19 — CENTRAL VENOUS ACCESS: THE CONSUMABLE RESOURCE
       ============================================================ */
    subgraph cluster_CVC {
        label=<<B>19. Central venous access as a CONSUMABLE resource</B><BR/><FONT POINT-SIZE="8">there are only so many veins; running out of them is what forces transplantation</FONT>>;
        style="filled"; fillcolor="#f7f0f0"; color="#8a2020"; fontsize=11;
        node [shape=ellipse, fillcolor="#f0d5d5", color="#8a2020"];

        V_CATHDAY  [label="Cumulative catheter-days", fillcolor="#e6bcbc"];
        V_CRBSI    [label="Catheter-related bloodstream\ninfection CRBSI\n~0.5-2 episodes /\n1000 catheter-days", fillcolor="#e6bcbc"];
        V_ORG      [label="Causative organisms\nCoNS · S. aureus · Candida ·\nenteric Gram-negatives\n(translocation)"];
        V_SEPSIS   [label="Sepsis, hospitalisation", shape=diamond, fillcolor="#e6d0ea", color="#6a3a8a"];
        V_THROMB   [label="Catheter-related thrombosis"];
        V_STENOS   [label="Venous stenosis / occlusion"];
        V_ACCESS   [label="Patent central veins remaining\n(6 → 0)", fillcolor="#e6bcbc"];
        V_ACCLOSS  [label="LOSS OF VENOUS ACCESS\n— an indication for transplant", shape=diamond, fillcolor="#e6d0ea", color="#6a3a8a"];
        V_MECH     [label="Mechanical complications\nocclusion, breakage,\ndislodgement"];
        V_TECHNIQUE[label="Aseptic technique,\ndedicated HPN team\n(largest single risk modifier)", shape=ellipse, fillcolor="#dcecdc", color="#4a7a4a"];
        V_CYCLE    [label="Weekly cycling\ncatheter-free interval"];

        P_PNVOL -> V_CATHDAY; P_DAYSWK -> V_CATHDAY;
        V_CATHDAY -> V_CRBSI; V_CRBSI -> V_ORG; V_CRBSI -> V_SEPSIS;
        V_CRBSI -> V_THROMB -> V_STENOS -> V_ACCESS [arrowhead=odiamond];
        V_ACCESS -> V_ACCLOSS [arrowhead=odiamond];
        V_TECHNIQUE -> V_CRBSI [arrowhead=odiamond, color="#2f7f2f", penwidth=1.4];
        V_CYCLE -> V_CRBSI [arrowhead=odiamond, color="#2f7f2f"];
        V_MECH -> V_ACCESS [arrowhead=odiamond];
        G_ENDOTOX -> V_ORG [label="gut-origin\norganisms", style=dashed];
        V_SEPSIS -> H_INFLAM [color="#b03030", label="each episode\nadvances IFALD"];
    }

    /* ============================================================
       CLUSTER 20 — RENAL, STONE AND BONE COMPLICATIONS
       ============================================================ */
    subgraph cluster_RENAL {
        label=<<B>20. Renal, stone and metabolic bone disease</B><BR/><FONT POINT-SIZE="8">enteric hyperoxaluria REQUIRES a colon; end-jejunostomy patients get dehydration stones instead</FONT>>;
        style="filled"; fillcolor="#eef2f8"; color="#3a4a8a"; fontsize=11;
        node [shape=ellipse, fillcolor="#d5ddf0", color="#3a4a8a"];

        Y_FATFA    [label="Unabsorbed fatty acids\nbind luminal Ca²⁺"];
        Y_FREEOX   [label="Free (unbound) oxalate"];
        Y_COLPERM  [label="Colonic oxalate permeability ↑\n(bile acids & FA injure mucosa)"];
        Y_HYPEROX  [label="ENTERIC HYPEROXALURIA\n(needs a colon!)", fillcolor="#f5d9d9", color="#a04040"];
        Y_STONE    [label="Calcium oxalate nephrolithiasis", shape=diamond, fillcolor="#e6d0ea", color="#6a3a8a"];
        Y_OXALNEPH [label="Oxalate nephropathy → CKD", fillcolor="#f5d9d9", color="#a04040"];
        Y_DEHYDST  [label="Dehydration / low-citrate stones\n(the end-jejunostomy pattern)"];
        Y_CKD      [label="CKD (up to ~40% of long-term HPN)", shape=diamond, fillcolor="#e6d0ea", color="#6a3a8a"];
        Y_MGLOSS   [label="Magnesium depletion\n(ileum-dependent)", fillcolor="#f5d9d9", color="#a04040"];
        Y_PTHRES   [label="Mg deficiency → impaired PTH\nsecretion AND end-organ resistance"];
        Y_HYPOCA   [label="Hypocalcaemia\n— refractory until Mg replaced", shape=doubleoctagon, fillcolor="#f3c9c9", color="#8b1a1a", penwidth=2];
        Y_VITD     [label="Vitamin D deficiency (fat-soluble)\n25-OH vitamin D"];
        Y_ACIDOSIS [label="Chronic metabolic acidosis\n(bicarbonate loss)"];
        Y_MBD      [label="Metabolic bone disease:\nosteomalacia + osteoporosis", shape=diamond, fillcolor="#e6d0ea", color="#6a3a8a"];
        Y_ALUM     [label="Aluminium contamination of PN"];
        Y_BMD      [label="Bone mineral density T-score", shape=diamond, fillcolor="#e6d0ea", color="#6a3a8a"];

        C_FRACFAT -> Y_FATFA [arrowhead=odiamond]; Y_FATFA -> Y_FREEOX;
        B_LOSS -> Y_COLPERM; Y_FATFA -> Y_COLPERM;
        Y_FREEOX -> Y_HYPEROX; Y_COLPERM -> Y_HYPEROX; A_COLON -> Y_HYPEROX [label="requires colon", style=dashed];
        Y_HYPEROX -> R_OXAL; R_OXAL -> Y_STONE; Y_HYPEROX -> Y_OXALNEPH -> Y_CKD;
        W_DEHYD -> Y_DEHYDST -> Y_STONE; W_DEHYD -> Y_CKD; R_AKI -> Y_CKD;
        Y_MGLOSS -> Y_PTHRES -> Y_HYPOCA;
        F_MGAB -> Y_MGLOSS [arrowhead=odiamond];
        Y_VITD -> F_CAAB [arrowhead=odiamond]; C_FRACFAT -> Y_VITD;
        Y_VITD -> Y_MBD; Y_ACIDOSIS -> Y_MBD; Y_ALUM -> Y_MBD; Y_HYPOCA -> Y_MBD;
        Y_MBD -> Y_BMD [arrowhead=odiamond];
        Y_ACIDOSIS -> Y_STONE [label="citrate ↓"];
    }

    /* ============================================================
       CLUSTER 21 — MICRONUTRIENT DEFICITS
       ============================================================ */
    subgraph cluster_MICRO2 {
        label=<<B>21. Micronutrient deficits — site-specific, not generic</B><BR/><FONT POINT-SIZE="8">each deficiency maps to a named resected segment or a named stool loss</FONT>>;
        style="filled"; fillcolor="#f7f4ec"; color="#7a6a20"; fontsize=11;
        node [shape=ellipse, fillcolor="#eee7cd", color="#7a6a20"];

        X_B12      [label="Vitamin B12 — terminal ileum ONLY\n→ SC/IM replacement obligatory"];
        X_FOLATE   [label="Folate — jejunal"];
        X_IRON     [label="Iron — duodenum/proximal jejunum"];
        X_ZN       [label="Zinc — lost in stool/stoma output\n(~12 mg/L)"];
        X_SE       [label="Selenium (myocardium · thyroid)\n— cardiomyopathy risk"];
        X_CU       [label="Copper (biliary excretion,\nstoma losses)"];
        X_VITA     [label="Vitamin A (night blindness)"];
        X_VITE     [label="Vitamin E (neuropathy)"];
        X_VITK     [label="Vitamin K (coagulation · bone)"];
        X_THIAM    [label="Thiamine (Wernicke risk)\n— days of reserve only", fillcolor="#f5d9d9", color="#a04040"];
        X_EFA      [label="Essential fatty acids\n(linoleic · α-linolenic)"];
        X_CARNIT   [label="Carnitine"];
        X_ANEMIA   [label="Anaemia (combined B12 ·\nfolate · iron)", shape=diamond, fillcolor="#e6d0ea", color="#6a3a8a"];
        X_NEURO    [label="Neurological deficits\n(B12 · E · copper · thiamine)", shape=diamond, fillcolor="#e6d0ea", color="#6a3a8a"];

        A_ILEUM -> X_B12 [arrowhead=odiamond]; G_B12CONS -> X_B12 [arrowhead=odiamond];
        C_FRACFAT -> X_VITA [arrowhead=odiamond]; C_FRACFAT -> X_VITE [arrowhead=odiamond];
        C_FRACFAT -> X_VITK [arrowhead=odiamond]; C_FRACFAT -> Y_VITD [arrowhead=odiamond];
        W_OUTPUT -> X_ZN [arrowhead=odiamond, label="12 mg per L"];
        W_OUTPUT -> Y_MGLOSS [label="Mg lost in output"];
        I_LIPIDMIN -> X_EFA [arrowhead=odiamond];
        X_B12 -> X_ANEMIA [arrowhead=odiamond]; X_FOLATE -> X_ANEMIA [arrowhead=odiamond];
        X_IRON -> X_ANEMIA [arrowhead=odiamond];
        X_B12 -> X_NEURO [arrowhead=odiamond]; X_VITE -> X_NEURO [arrowhead=odiamond];
        X_CU -> X_NEURO [arrowhead=odiamond]; X_THIAM -> X_NEURO [arrowhead=odiamond];
        X_ZN -> D_CRYPT [label="Zn required for\ncrypt mitosis", style=dashed];
        X_CARNIT -> I_STEATO [arrowhead=odiamond, style=dashed];
    }

    /* ============================================================
       CLUSTER 22 — CLINICAL ENDPOINTS
       ============================================================ */
    subgraph cluster_ENDP {
        label=<<B>22. Clinical endpoints</B><BR/><FONT POINT-SIZE="8">the registered endpoint (≥20% PN volume reduction) is a property of the weaning algorithm, not of a score</FONT>>;
        style="filled"; fillcolor="#f5f0f8"; color="#5a2a8a"; fontsize=11;
        node [shape=diamond, fillcolor="#e6d0ea", color="#5a2a8a"];

        Z_PNVOL    [label="Weekly PN volume (L/week)", fillcolor="#d5b8e0"];
        Z_RESP20   [label="Responders with ≥20% PN\nvolume reduction\n(STEPS primary endpoint)", fillcolor="#d5b8e0"];
        Z_DAYSOFF  [label="Days per week off PN"];
        Z_AUTON    [label="ENTERAL AUTONOMY\n(complete weaning off PN)", fillcolor="#c9a8d8"];
        Z_OUTPUT   [label="Stool / stoma output (L/day)"];
        Z_CITR     [label="Plasma citrulline (µmol/L)\n<20 predicts PN dependence"];
        Z_WT       [label="Body weight, BMI"];
        Z_QOL      [label="Quality of life (SBS-QoL)"];
        Z_INFEC    [label="CRBSI episodes/year"];
        Z_LIVER    [label="Liver: bilirubin, fibrosis stage"];
        Z_SURV     [label="Survival on HPN\n(5-year ~70-80%)", fillcolor="#c9a8d8"];
        Z_TX       [label="Intestinal / combined\nliver-intestine transplant", fillcolor="#c9a8d8"];
        Z_TXFREE   [label="Transplant-free survival"];
        Z_HOSP     [label="Hospital days per year"];

        P_PNVOL -> Z_PNVOL; Z_PNVOL -> Z_RESP20; P_DAYSWK -> Z_DAYSOFF;
        Z_DAYSOFF -> Z_AUTON; Z_PNVOL -> Z_AUTON [arrowhead=odiamond];
        W_OUTPUT -> Z_OUTPUT; D_MUCMASS -> Z_CITR; N_WEIGHT -> Z_WT;
        Z_PNVOL -> Z_QOL [arrowhead=odiamond]; Z_AUTON -> Z_QOL;
        V_CRBSI -> Z_INFEC; I_BILI -> Z_LIVER; I_FIB -> Z_LIVER;
        Z_LIVER -> Z_TX [color="#b03030"]; Z_LIVER -> Z_SURV [arrowhead=odiamond];
        Z_INFEC -> Z_SURV [arrowhead=odiamond]; Z_INFEC -> Z_HOSP;
        Z_TX -> Z_TXFREE [arrowhead=odiamond]; Z_SURV -> Z_TXFREE;
        Y_CKD -> Z_SURV [arrowhead=odiamond]; Y_BMD -> Z_QOL [arrowhead=odiamond];
        G_ENCEPH -> Z_QOL [arrowhead=odiamond]; X_ANEMIA -> Z_QOL [arrowhead=odiamond];
        A_TYPE1 -> Z_AUTON [arrowhead=odiamond, style=dashed, label="anatomical floor:\nno drug crosses it"];
    }


    /* ============================================================
       CROSS-CLUSTER EDGES
       Declared here, after every cluster, so that each node is claimed
       by the cluster that DEFINES it rather than by whichever cluster
       happens to mention it first.
       ============================================================ */
    L_GHRELIN  -> N_HYPERPH  [label="hyperphagia drive", style=dashed];
    G_ENDOTOX  -> H_INFLAM   [color="#b03030"];
    W_DEHYD    -> R_AKI      [color="#b03030"];
    P_ILE      -> I_PHYTO    [label="the lipid emulsion\nIS the dose"];
    T_CITRISE  -> Z_CITR     [style=dotted];
    R_CHOLINE  -> I_CHOLINE  [arrowhead=odiamond, color="#2f7f2f"];
    R_ABXLOCK  -> V_CRBSI    [arrowhead=odiamond, color="#2f7f2f", penwidth=1.5];
    I_PHTN     -> Z_SURV     [color="#b03030"];
    V_ACCLOSS  -> Z_TX       [color="#b03030", penwidth=1.5];
    X_SE       -> Z_SURV     [style=dashed];

    /* ============================================================
       THE SELF-SUSTAINING POSITIVE FEEDBACK LOOP (drawn in bold red)
       ============================================================ */
    edge [color="#c01818", penwidth=2.2, arrowsize=0.9, fontcolor="#c01818"];
    L_BLUNTED -> M_BRAKE  [label="1. no ileal brake", arrowhead=odiamond];
    M_BRAKE   -> M_TRANSIT [label="2. transit accelerates", arrowhead=odiamond];
    M_TRANSIT -> C_CONTACT [label="3. contact time falls", arrowhead=odiamond];
    C_CONTACT -> C_DAMK    [label="4. Da falls"];
    C_DAMK    -> W_OUTPUT  [label="5. output rises"];
    W_OUTPUT  -> L_MASS    [label="6. unabsorbed load bypasses\nthe L-cells that are gone", arrowhead=odiamond, style=dashed];

    /* ============================================================
       LEGEND
       ============================================================ */
    subgraph cluster_LEGEND {
        label=<<B>Legend</B>>;
        style="filled"; fillcolor="#fafafa"; color="#999999"; fontsize=11;
        node [fontsize=8];
        LG1 [shape=box, fillcolor="#cfe0ef", color="#3f6d99", label="anatomy / parameter\n(not a state)"];
        LG2 [shape=ellipse, fillcolor="#e8e8e8", color="#666666", label="physiological flux / pool"];
        LG3 [shape=ellipse, fillcolor="#dcecdc", color="#4a7a4a", label="adaptive / protective"];
        LG4 [shape=ellipse, fillcolor="#f5d9d9", color="#a04040", label="maladaptive / injurious"];
        LG5 [shape=hexagon, fillcolor="#fbd9bf", color="#a04a10", label="drug / prescribed input"];
        LG6 [shape=diamond, fillcolor="#e6d0ea", color="#6a3a8a", label="clinical endpoint"];
        LG7 [shape=octagon, fillcolor="#f6e3a0", color="#a08000", label="conservation-equation node"];
        LG8 [shape=doubleoctagon, fillcolor="#f3c9c9", color="#8b1a1a", label="structural null or trap\n(effect must be ZERO or REVERSE)"];
        LG9 [shape=plaintext, fillcolor="#fafafa", label="bold red = self-sustaining\npositive feedback loop"];
        LG1 -> LG2 -> LG3 -> LG4 [style=invis];
        LG5 -> LG6 -> LG7 -> LG8 -> LG9 [style=invis];
    }
}
